WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.176
The AI industry is flooded with spectacular pitches and flawless tech demos.

2
00:00:05.226 --> 00:00:10.196
But when these models meet real business operations, most simply shatter.

3
00:00:10.246 --> 00:00:19.480
This graph shows the survival rate of new AI projects: a massive drop-off between a working prototype and a live production deployment.

4
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.950
Failures happen in this gap — unexpected edge cases, clunky APIs,

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.881
and unpredictable customers.

6
00:00:25.931 --> 00:00:30.916
Businesses do not need expensive novelties. They need AI that earns rent.

7
00:00:30.966 --> 00:00:38.157
They require systems built specifically to generate a measurable return on investment, month after month.

8
00:00:38.207 --> 00:00:47.950
Getting an AI tool to survive in the wild means focusing on the unglamorous 20% of software development: optimising Core Web Vitals for speed,

9
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.312
configuring strict right-to-left Arabic text formatting, and programming strict halal business rules.

10
00:00:54.362 --> 00:00:56.895
We have enough visionaries selling ideas.

11
00:00:56.945 --> 00:01:03.887
The market is starved for engineers who can ensure these complex systems actually survive contact with reality.

12
00:01:03.937 --> 00:01:11.950
Mohammad Makki is a full-stack developer and AI solutions architect who operates in direct opposition to the current hype cycle.

13
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.181
His philosophy is straightforward: he ships rather than pitches.

14
00:01:16.231 --> 00:01:21.405
He has deployed over 100 projects to real, active storefronts and live servers.

15
00:01:21.455 --> 00:01:30.000
As tech lead and co-founder of CommandNet Solutions, Makki oversees the conversion of raw machine learning into deployed commerce.

16
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:35.950
Inside his research and development layer — the lab — Makki engineers raw machine learning

17
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.748
into reliable business logic.

18
00:01:37.798 --> 00:01:41.841
He uses a technique called Retrieval-Augmented Generation, or RAG.

19
00:01:41.891 --> 00:01:49.283
It forces the AI to check a company's private, verified data and strict business rules before it generates any response.

20
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:55.051
This flow chart shows how he builds these systems using frameworks like LangChain and Claude.

21
00:01:55.101 --> 00:01:59.950
A central agent receives a user query, autonomously reaches into a database for

22
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.421
accurate context, and routes a decision to a specific software tool.

23
00:02:04.471 --> 00:02:12.377
These agents function as background engines, executing multi-step sequences to process data and trigger business actions.

24
00:02:12.427 --> 00:02:20.399
Engineering these rigorous back-end workflows separates a fragile AI gimmick from a reliable, autonomous digital employee.

25
00:02:20.449 --> 00:02:23.950
But business logic still needs a secure place to live.

26
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.773
Hosting and scaling AI operations safely requires heavy, specialised infrastructure.

27
00:02:28.823 --> 00:02:37.960
Makki deploys a full-stack architecture for enterprise clients: Python for backend logic, Postgres databases for massive data sets, and React for the interface.

28
00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.840
You can see it in action on the dashboard he built for the forex trading platform 4T.

29
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:47.950
The system manages high-stakes, real-time financial data with zero tolerance for latency.

30
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.937
He also designs and ships complete corporate platforms, like the end-to-end build for industrial supplier Chemigaz,

31
00:02:54.987 --> 00:03:00.041
or the generative AI ad campaigns running for the study-abroad platform CrossAbroad.

32
00:03:00.091 --> 00:03:09.459
The most intelligent language model available is useless unless it is routed through an enterprise infrastructure built to handle its computational weight.

33
00:03:09.509 --> 00:03:11.950
Once the secure backend infrastructure is

34
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:17.774
fully in place, the AI finally interacts directly with the consumer on the live storefront.

35
00:03:17.824 --> 00:03:25.198
Makki deploys recommendation engines and generative AI integrations directly into complex Shopify Plus environments.

36
00:03:25.248 --> 00:03:35.950
For the cosmetics brand Narins Beauty, he built and actively manages their AI support chatbot, with custom escalation flows that route difficult issues to human agents.

37
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:42.477
He also handles complex storefront operations for brands like Al Rugaib Furniture and Ferronato,

38
00:03:42.527 --> 00:03:49.684
navigating strict bilingual Arabic and English constraints and integrating advanced room visualiser tools.

39
00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:53.695
The ultimate test of this architecture is its invisibility.

40
00:03:53.745 --> 00:03:59.950
The technology drives engagement and generates revenue without the end user ever feeling the

41
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.787
massive underlying complexity.

42
00:04:01.837 --> 00:04:06.379
This level of execution requires commanding an incredibly broad tech stack.

43
00:04:06.429 --> 00:04:15.562
Makki controls everything from raw machine learning models and DevOps infrastructure at the bottom, all the way up to Tailwind CSS on a mobile screen.

44
00:04:15.612 --> 00:04:23.950
Owning the entire stack eliminates the operational friction and departmental miscommunication that traditionally kills software projects.

45
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:32.531
His process always begins with a rigorous business diagnosis, ensuring every line of code serves a strategic commercial purpose.

46
00:04:32.581 --> 00:04:42.788
As the technology matures, the companies that prioritise robust, scalable integrations will pull ahead of those left holding flashy, unusable prototypes.

47
00:04:42.838 --> 00:04:47.950
For enterprises looking to actually build and scale intelligent applications,

48
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:55.950
Mohammad Makki is the architect who makes sure the technology earns its keep.
